WEBVTT

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.750
<i>Escape</i>

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.920
<i>On this wind,</i>

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.630
<i>I let my tears ride</i>

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:16.810
<i>Speeding up until they dry</i>

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.520
<i>I can fly over and go on</i>

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.270
<i>I just know that the answer</i>

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:30.570
<i>Is out there, on the far side of that distant sky</i>

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:38.120
<i>In this place, where I can't find the answer</i>

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:43.420
<i>I sigh and look at the sky</i>

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:48.880
<i>Shining deep in these eyes suffused in blue</i>

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.760
<i>Is a dreamer, who can go anywhere</i>

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.130
<i>That's me, you see</i>

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.800
<i>Escape</i>

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.800
<i>On this wind,</i>

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.600
<i>I let my wish ride</i>

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.850
<i>My outstretched hands paint the future</i>

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.480
<i>I'm not afraid anymore</i>

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.280
<i>Of the trace of tears</i>

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:16.870
<i>Suffused in rainbow colors, I fly on</i>

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:25.420
<i>To the far side of that sky</i>

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.740
Looks like we're finally back

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.740
to being on routine standby.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.120
That's not even funny!

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.390
It isn't our job to pursue that terrorist.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.730
To destroy Secrets before

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.730
they detonate in a fusion blast.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.060
That is the mission of the IFO teams.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.650
We don't have the time

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.650
to take on any extra work.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:45.290
Now, now, you two, I think

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:45.290
that's enough of that.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.080
So, what's his penalty?

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.880
There is no precedent for this,

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.170
but I believe he should be punished severely.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.840
I think a stern reprimand

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.840
should do for this time around.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.340
That is going too easy on him!

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.590
Are you of the same opinion?

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.140
There's the matter of Team

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.140
Goldilocks to consider, too...

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:06.060
Then it's settled.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:10.400
I'm going to put my trust in you,

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:10.400
so there'll be no further punishment.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:11.610
What?

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:16.610
To me, IFO pilots are like

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:16.610
my own children, after all.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.240
It's part of a father's duty to give

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.240
his children the benefit of his trust.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.330
A father...

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:30.170
You have no right to say such things.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.760
--Hey, what's with that guy?

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.760
--I know!

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.540
"Fleur Blanc Official Blog

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.540
A Place to Connect"

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.630
Ao!

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.930
Shopping?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.640
Yeah.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.400
Hey! Sweetheart!

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.900
Get me a Generation coffee! Hot!

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.280
What's the big idea?

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.160
Why are you following me around?!

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.950
Oh, well, lemme think...

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.870
Just quit hanging around me already!

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.920
Was that his idea of being intimidating?

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.340
Are you monitoring Ao?

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.300
If you are, you should put

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.300
a little more thought into it.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.970
You're being way too obvious.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.350
That's what we've been told to do.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.190
You're blatantly monitoring him

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.190
to put pressure on him?!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.820
I find it hard to believe that this was your idea.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:26.740
Orders... from the CEO?

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:30.410
So I hear that you don't get

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:30.410
along with your old man?

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.330
--Ao's the same.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.330
--What?

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.710
Him and his old man...

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.610
We have a formal request.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.530
Mobilize at once.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:12.240
Roger that.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.290
Faisal Arabia, huh?

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.710
It certainly turned up in a troublesome spot.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.420
A telephone call from the

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.420
Allied Forces for the CEO.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:24.090
And speak of the devil.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.300
I'll take it in my office.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.220
Transfer the call for me.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:36.230
In Colombia, your team got taken out,

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.270
and the other day, you had that terrorist scare.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.060
You've taken one hit after

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.060
another there, Christophe.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:44.150
I appreciate your concern,

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:44.150
Mr. Secretary of State.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.110
Thinking about what I've got coming up

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.110
ahead makes my head hurt, too.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.910
Meaning?

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.450
It's that Nirvash of yours.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.790
Some of our congressmen have

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.790
begun fussing that it's the Mark I,

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:00.830
which was in our country's custody

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:00.830
until it went missing at some point.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:01.920
Oh?

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.090
It seems they're planning

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.090
to team up with the media

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:07.220
and put pressure on the President.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.800
The election is coming up, so they're

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.800
willing to do whatever it takes.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.600
I see.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:17.060
However, the Nirvash and the Mark I

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:17.060
are two completely different crafts.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:19.730
Yes, I know that.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:26.440
But for the United States government

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:26.440
to respect Generation Bleu's claim...

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:29.570
Faisal Arabia, is it?

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.040
It's still a ways out.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.790
Shall we make it our priority

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.790
to retrieve the Quartz?

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.550
What will you do if the

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.550
enemy increases its speed?

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.130
That's...

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.090
Since we've allowed for the Secret to appear,

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.720
there's only one course

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.720
of action we ought to take.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:58.480
H-Hold on a second.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.940
Then those guys were monitoring

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.940
me on orders from the CEO?

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.230
Probably.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:04.810
I see.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.990
After all that stuff he said

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.990
about trust and being a father...

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.660
The things he says and does

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.660
are totally inconsistent!

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.990
Oh, so he pulled that line on you, too.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:19.620
"The IFO pilots are my children."

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.080
He's got some nerve saying that

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.080
in front of his own daughter.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.000
--Daughter?

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.000
--Oh? Did we never tell you?

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.680
Fleur is our CEO's daughter.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:34.220
Wha... What?!

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:35.720
That's enough chitchat.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.850
We've identified the Secret.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.430
This Secret closely resembles the one

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:47.400
that was sighted in 1752 in Philadelphia, USA.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.200
Apparently, when the Secret

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.200
appeared on that occasion,

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:56.160
the surrounding area suffered damage

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:56.160
caused by a series of lightning strikes.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.870
When you get down to it,

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.870
the phenomenon called lightning

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.040
occurs when a difference in

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.040
electric potential arises in space

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.540
that exceeds the dielectric strength of air--

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:05.460
The mission is cancelled.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.170
The Triton will return immediately.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:09.960
What in the world happened?!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.210
CEO's orders.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.680
What? The CEO?!

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.680
What kind of order is that?!

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.140
Reverse course.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.100
Chief?! You can't be...

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.140
Chief?! Chief!

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:22.980
--Chief!

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:22.980
--Roger that.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.160
Yes, it's me.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.750
Some kind of deal was struck behind the scenes.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.250
That's the only thing I can think of.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:50.750
If so, about the only entity that

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:50.750
can put pressure on our CEO

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.550
is probably the United States government.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:55.470
Why would America do that?

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.100
Faisal Arabia, where the

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.100
Scub turned up this time,

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.770
is the most anti-US country

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.770
in all of the Middle East.

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:04.810
And the US deems Faisal Arabia to

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:04.810
have aided terrorist organizations

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:06.770
and regards them with hostility,

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:08.310
so the two countries are in a situation

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.770
where war could break out

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.770
between them at any time.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:13.940
Faisal Arabia's thoroughly anti-US sentiments

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.820
grew out of conflict within the

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.820
royal family of former Saudi Arabia...

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.530
If the fusion blast is allowed to occur,

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:23.290
it will be a serious blow to their enemy

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:27.120
and also prevent the establishment

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:27.120
of a Coral plant. That's why.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:28.420
You've got to be kidding me!

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:31.800
Why would our CEO go along

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:31.800
with something like that?!

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.380
Probably because he was

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.380
presented with conditions

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.760
that would be profitable for the company.

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:37.800
You're wrong about that! I'm sure he--

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:39.550
Rebecka!

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:45.890
Telling us to go back now

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:45.890
means he expects us...

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.780
...to stand by and watch people die!

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:14.630
Fleur?!

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.550
Are they eloping?!

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:51.170
I hate my father.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.000
You hate yours, too, right?

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.130
I heard about it from Mr. Gazelle and his gang.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.180
Maybe that makes us alike.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:03.470
--It doesn't make any sense.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:03.470
--What?

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:07.220
Why do you work for the company

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:07.220
run by the father you hate?

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:17.070
Five years ago, my maman and I

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:17.070
were caught in a traffic accident.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:23.870
With transplant surgery using

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:23.870
the organs we had between us,

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.660
one of us could be saved.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:28.910
When my father was told this by the doctor,

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:32.370
he chose me and killed my maman.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:38.000
I loved my maman.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:42.380
If I'd died then, she probably would be...

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:53.140
I despise my father for burdening me with this.

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:57.770
That's why I do what he least wants me to do.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:07.870
Chief...

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:16.250
These are scenes from within

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:16.250
the country of Faisal Arabia.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.800
This footage was taken in the suburbs

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.800
of Abuha, the old state capital,

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:23.090
where the G-Monster appeared.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:26.260
--In light of this...

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:26.260
--Both of you get back right away.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:29.010
Because of this footage, cries have

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:29.010
gone up all across the globe

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:32.180
that aid should be given to Faisal Arabia.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.810
It seems the Allied Forces had no

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.810
choice but to endorse it as well.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:37.230
Then...!

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:39.520
The order to return has been rescinded.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.690
We're resuming the mission.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.000
I'm not going to let those

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.000
bastards get their way!

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.870
I'll show them!

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:54.870
America and our stupid CEO, too!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.830
Our stupid CEO!

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.520
We've got even more reason not

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.520
to lose than usual, Miss Fleur!

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:15.440
You said it, Ao!

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.190
You guys are kind of fired up.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:20.270
Wanna just go for it and "combine"?

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:21.980
Huh?!

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:26.400
180 seconds to combat airspace.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.200
Target acquired.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.030
Putting it up on the screen.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:33.160
That lightning is nothing

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:33.160
more than a phenomenon

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.750
resulting from the charged

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.750
particles released by the Secret.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.460
Because lFOs are enveloped in trapar,

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.460
Secrets ordinarily do not attack them.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:46.300
However, in this case, the lightning

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:46.300
is independent of the Secret's will

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:50.340
and is merely electricity being

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:50.340
discharged, so please be careful.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.010
The lightning can also occur outside the ZOA.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:58.440
lFOs have electromagnetic shields

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:58.440
as a countermeasure against lightning,

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:00.310
but in the event of a direct strike,

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:02.860
there is a chance that the system will go down.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.650
Please be careful of this as well.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.820
You keep telling us to be careful,

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.820
but specifically, what should we do?

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:10.160
Please avoid them.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:11.990
He makes it sound so simple, daccha.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:14.950
Didn't I tell you to dial it back during combat?

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.910
Let's get going soon.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.510
You'll be outside the discharge zone there.

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:29.260
The Hot Summer of Ukraine at full power!

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.110
Again!

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.530
The amount of charged particles being released

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.540
is increasing at a rate of 250% per second.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:58.330
--Discharge zone is expanding.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:58.330
--All lFOs retreat!

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:09.760
No way!

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.930
Oh, man...

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.050
Elena, come in! Elena!

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.310
Nirvash and Alleluia, stand by where you are.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:21.100
--But...!

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:21.100
--Without the Kyrie, this operation can't succeed.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:23.400
Chief, the Secret!

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.870
The Secret has released all the

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.870
charged particles it had accumulated

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:40.910
and has begun to gain altitude.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.670
75 seconds from now, it will lose thrust.

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.380
It is anticipated that it will crash.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:46.960
Estimated location of the crash is...

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.380
The Scub Coral?!

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:51.090
No! Don't tell me it's going

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:51.090
to smash itself into it?!

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:53.630
The operation is canceled! Take cover at once!

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:57.260
--What?!

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:57.260
--The situation has changed. We have no choice.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:17:00.100
--Damn.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:17:00.100
--Don't say we have no choice!

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.440
If we leave it at this, we lose.

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:06.110
And losing to those bastards

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:06.110
is out of the question!

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.610
Listen to me. You need to

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.610
start by calming down, Ao.

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:11.030
But...!

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.450
Miss Fleur?! Miss Fleur!

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.280
Fleur, get back here! Fleur!

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:20.160
115 seconds until fusion blast.

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:33.590
Miss Fleur, please respond! Miss Fleur!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:38.930
There's no way the Alleluia's

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:38.930
firepower will be enough, so...

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:40.930
This is the one fight I don't want to lose.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:42.020
What?

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:46.310
For me, this is the one

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:46.310
fight I don't want to lose.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.730
No matter what happens to me.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:53.320
Secret has arrived at an altitude

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:53.320
of 7,200 feet over Faisal Arabia.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:55.320
It has lost thrust.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:57.570
Commencing descent.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.990
I'm not okay with that.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:04.330
I hate my dad, too.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.210
But...

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:09.460
...I won't risk my life for a bastard like him.

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:10.670
I'm going to live through this...

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.300
Live through it all no matter what,

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:15.340
and punch him real good!

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:16.760
So, Fleur!

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.800
You can't die, either!

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:28.980
There's no time.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:30.610
Here we go, Fleur!

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:32.320
Okay!

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.080
Nirvash and Alleluia have

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.080
latched on to the Secret.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.290
25 seconds remaining to fusion blast.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:08.060
Ten... Nine... Eight... Seven...

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:11.940
Six... Five... Four... Three...

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.440
Two... One...

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:25.410
Georg, what about Alleluia and Nirvash?

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:28.410
Alleluia and Nirvash are both in good shape.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:30.920
We also have confirmed life signs,

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.460
so I believe the pilots are fine as well.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:41.930
Fleur, are you okay?

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.640
Yes.

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:47.310
I'm alive.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:54.020
Yeah, we're alive.

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:01.610
Where are you two going?

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:03.160
To see our stupid CEO!

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.660
We need to report our victory to him!

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:08.660
I can't wait to see the look on his face.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:11.420
Maybe he'll be crying after

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:11.420
getting chewed out by America.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:15.630
I wonder how our stupid CEO

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:15.630
will look when he greets us.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.630
Ow-ow-ow!

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:20.630
Stop yanking on it!

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:25.140
--Ow!

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:25.140
--Wow, it's got some real sticking power.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:27.100
Hey, they're back.

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:30.850
Oh, hey! What do you think?!

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:30.850
I look pretty good, huh?!

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:45.030
Those outfits...

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:57.380
You left your posts without permission

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:57.380
in the middle of an active operation.

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:01.300
I have a couple questions for

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:01.300
you regarding that incident.

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:06.680
After playing that footage, a report

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:06.680
went out from goodness knows where

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.510
that we had yet to arrive on site

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:13.980
in spite of the fact that we'd

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:13.980
received a formal request to mobilize.

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:16.520
I immediately got a call from America.

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:19.690
It seems they thought that the

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:19.690
information had come from us.

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:20.690
And?

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:24.110
Of course, my response was,

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:24.110
"I have no knowledge of that."

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:32.620
By the way, why did you stay on-site

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:32.620
even after you'd been ordered to return?

00:21:32.870 --> 00:21:34.500
Engine trouble.

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:36.750
I had a hell of a time repairing it.

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:42.210
Where to?

00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:44.430
The children are waiting.

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:48.260
It was the CEO who made that footage...

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:51.350
That bastard deceived the world, you know.

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:54.520
But thanks to that,

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:54.520
we were allowed to mobilize.

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:57.270
We were able to save lots of lives.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.150
Fleur...

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:03.530
Did we win?

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:08.240
Hey, since when do you get off

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:08.240
addressing me so casually?!

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:09.950
What?

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:28.840
"To Be Continued"

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:28.510
To be continued!

00:22:30.930 --> 00:22:35.310
<i>The pounding beat of my heart</i>

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:42.270
<i>Had become a familiar part</i>

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:42.270
<i>of me before I knew it</i>

00:22:42.530 --> 00:22:48.200
<i>Even if there's a stiff wind blowing</i>

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:54.330
<i>I'll always be looking ahead, eyes wide open</i>

00:22:54.580 --> 00:23:01.920
<i>If you ever feel like crying, remember</i>

00:23:02.170 --> 00:23:07.970
<i>The promise we silently swore to one another</i>

00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:14.010
<i>The song of a fledgling taking wing</i>

00:23:14.270 --> 00:23:19.600
<i>Even now, still unable to fly well</i>

00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:25.610
<i>But over time that comes and goes</i>

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:27.820
<i>Single-mindedly</i>

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:31.160
<i>Following those joined hands</i>

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:37.160
<i>"So I never let you go!!" Those words</i>

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:42.840
<i>Even if they only vanish into the sky</i>

00:23:43.090 --> 00:23:48.880
<i>Inside the scattering lights</i>

00:23:49.130 --> 00:23:51.010
<i>Unwaveringly</i>

00:23:51.260 --> 00:23:56.600
<i>I know I can find you</i>

00:23:59.060 --> 00:24:02.860
"Preview"

00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:06.030
Next time on <i>Eureka Seven AO.</i>

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:09.610
Desiring radical change in order

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:09.610
to bring about something new,

00:24:09.860 --> 00:24:11.860
a youth summons a relic of the past.

00:24:12.110 --> 00:24:14.030
A thing appears in the

00:24:12.110 --> 00:24:14.030
pitch-black depths of the water.

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:16.200
What in the world will it offer the youth?

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:18.750
And what in the world will it show the boy?

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:24.170
<i>Eureka Seven AO</i>, Episode 9.

00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:26.500
Hear the cry of the children of the stars.
